{"name":"Knightcore","title":"Knightcore","revision":236170,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Knightcore","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Knightcore is an aesthetic inspired by medieval knights. It has a large presence on social platforms like Tumblr and is characterized by themes of combat and nature visuals. There is also often overlap with Medieval Fantasy, as opposed to being based solely on historical knights."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Due to their practical purposes, historically accurate and historically-inspired knight attire is generally uncomfortable and regarded as inappropriate for everyday wear and most formal occasions. They are mostly used in art and cosplay."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This aesthetic often utilizes modern interpretations of Medieval armor, as opposed to historically accurate depictions of it."},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather"},{"kind":"list","text":"Metal armor"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gauntlets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chainmail"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vests"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cloaks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crowns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jewelry, especially rings"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sheaths"},{"kind":"list","text":"Swords"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shields"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Practical"},{"kind":"list","text":"Layering (eg. firm fabrics on soft)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tucked shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather"},{"kind":"list","text":"Metal"},{"kind":"list","text":"Headpieces, eg. small crowns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sun and moon designs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Corsets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Puff sleeves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vests"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gloves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Belts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Buckles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jewelry, especially rings and bracelets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Boots"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chains"},{"kind":"list","text":"Small bags and pouches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Simplistic"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"list","text":"Horse-back riding"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fencing/Swordfighting"},{"kind":"list","text":"Archery"},{"kind":"list","text":"Running"},{"kind":"list","text":"Protecting/Bodyguarding"},{"kind":"list","text":"Practice fights"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Knightcore uses visuals similar to other Royalcore sub-aesthetics, but differs in its focus on knighthood, war, and adventure. Here is a short list of common Knightcore visuals:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wide, open skies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fields"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crosses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Palaces and castles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Medieval marketplaces"},{"kind":"list","text":"Horses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Metal, especially armor"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chainmail"},{"kind":"list","text":"Swords"},{"kind":"list","text":"Daggers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shields"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather"},{"kind":"list","text":"Flags, especially medieval flags"},{"kind":"list","text":"Symbolic imagery"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fire"},{"kind":"list","text":"Blood"},{"kind":"list","text":"Forests, especially during autumn and winter"},{"kind":"list","text":"Conflict/War"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Written Works"},{"kind":"list","text":"Krzyżacy (Knights of the Teutonic Order) by Henryk Sienkiewicz"},{"kind":"list","text":"Grażyna by Adam Mickiewicz"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ivanhoe by Walter Scott"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Once and Future King by T. H. White"},{"kind":"list","text":"Swordheart by T. Kingfisher"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Second Death of Locke by V. L. Bovalino"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Knight and the Moth by Rachel Gillig"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tortall Universe by Tamara Pierce"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Films"},{"kind":"list","text":"A Knight's Tale (2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Braveheart (1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Monty Python and the Holy Grail (1975)"},{"kind":"list","text":"El Cid (1961)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Green Knight (2021)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Messenger: The Story of Joan of Arc (1999)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Knight Before Christmas (2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Tale of Despareaux (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Excalibur (1981)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Snow White and the Huntsman (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Seventh Seal (1957)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Last Duel (2021)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The King (2019)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"TV Shows"},{"kind":"list","text":"Galavant (2015-2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Prince Valiant (1991-1993)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Knightmare (1987-1994)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Merlin (2008-2012"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Defender of the Crown (1986)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Heroes of Might and Magic (1995-2003)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Knightmare (1986)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shalom: Knightmare III' (1987)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Neopets: The Darkest Faerie (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chivalry: Medieval Warfare (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Demon's Souls (2009-2010/2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dark Souls (2011-2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"For Honor (2017)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Half Sword (2026)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kingdom Come: Deliverance (2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kingdom Come: Deliverance 2 (2025)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Medievil (1998, 2019)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Knightcore includes performances of songs composed from the Medieval period to the Renaissance and modern songs created in the Medieval style. It features instruments such as the lute, violin, and choir voices."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Songs"},{"kind":"list","text":"By the Sword - Emilie Autumn"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Bands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Blind Guardian"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jethro Tull"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rush (Caress of Steel, A Farewell to Kings)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Accounts"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Tumblr"},{"kind":"list","text":"ofswordsandarmor"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/0e/MonicaVitti.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20240514150018","caption":"MonicaVitti","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:MonicaVitti.jpeg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0562-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/09/Knight_5.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20201017003415","caption":"Knightcore · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Knight_5.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0562-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}